declarations.documentation:
The string @target@ holds, or @fallback@ when it holds anything else — including the `null` an absent
`field` answers. @fallback@ defaults to `""`, so the ordinary degrade-to-empty read needs no argument;
give it a placeholder to tell an absent field from one holding `""`.

@base@ raised to the @exponent@ power, as a `number`: a negative or fractional @exponent@ takes an
integer @base@ off the integers, so the type cannot promise integer — floor the result when an integer
is wanted. A non-finite result (0 to a negative power, a negative base to a fractional power) panics.

A named OAuth credential, stored server-side. The runtime injects and refreshes its tokens itself;
the name is not a secret. While the name has no usable credential, any use pauses the run on a
`prelude.oauth.authorize` escalation — answering it establishes the credential and resumes the run.

